# PostHog — publishable project API key (client-safe; ships in the client bundle).
# Find it in PostHog → Project Settings → Project API Key (starts with `phc_`).
#
# CI/prod: injected at BUILD time from a GitHub Actions secret
#   (NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY) so Next inlines it. The build runs in GH Actions
#   (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`), NOT on Vercel, so the key lives in GH secrets
#   — not Vercel env. Events post to the same-origin `/relay` path, which
#   `vercel.json` reverse-proxies to PostHog US so ad-blocker filter lists (which
#   match *.posthog.com) don't fire.
# Local dev: NOT required. The `/relay` proxy only exists on the Vercel deploy, so
#   analytics is verified on a preview deploy; local dev intentionally stays inert
#   when this is unset. (Set it in `.env.local` if you want posthog-js to init.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
